      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "ESG is not a threat to a company's core purpose; it's an evolution of it. The traditional shareholder-first model is outdated because it ignores the interconnectedness of modern business with society and the environment. Companies that fail to adapt risk becoming irrelevant. ESG isn't about social engineering; it's about recognizing that long-term shareholder value is inextricably linked to the well-being of the planet and its people. Ignoring this reality is a recipe for disaster. The real danger lies in clinging to an outdated model that doesn't account for the systemic risks and opportunities presented by our changing world. ESG is the future, and companies that embrace it will lead the way.",
      "source": "target",
